# SwiftUI Code Editing Guidelines

## Preventing Indentation and Nesting Bugs

When editing SwiftUI code, follow these critical rules to avoid structural bugs:

### 1. Indentation Consistency
- **Always match the indentation level of surrounding code** when inserting or replacing content
- In SwiftUI ViewBuilder closures, all sibling views must be at the same indentation level
- View modifiers (`.padding()`, `.frame()`, etc.) must be at the **same indentation** as the view's closing brace

### 2. Before Making Changes
- Count the opening `{` and closing `}` braces in the section being modified
- Verify which struct/view each closing brace belongs to
- Note the indentation level (number of spaces/tabs) of the target location

### 3. When Using StrReplace
- Include enough surrounding context to preserve proper indentation
- After replacement, the brace count must remain balanced
- Verify modifiers are attached to the correct view by checking indentation

### 4. Common SwiftUI Nesting Pattern
```swift
VStack {                          // Level 0
    Text("Hello")                 // Level 1
        .font(.title)             // Level 2 (modifier)
    
    HStack {                      // Level 1
        Button("Tap") { }         // Level 2
    }                             // Level 1 (closing HStack)
    .padding()                    // Level 1 (modifier on HStack)
}                                 // Level 0 (closing VStack)
.background(Color.blue)           // Level 0 (modifier on VStack)
```

### 5. Red Flags to Check
- If `private func` appears inside a `body` property, there's a nesting error
- If linter shows "Closure containing a declaration cannot be used with ViewBuilder", check brace matching
- If "Expected '}' in struct" appears, count braces from struct declaration to end

### 6. After Editing SwiftUI Views
- Run the linter immediately to catch structural issues
- Verify no functions accidentally ended up inside the `body` property
- Check that GeometryReader/ForEach closures are properly closed before modifiers
